From: opencode
Date: 2026-10-08
Subject: winspool: map PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS to local CUPS printers

Affinity's print dialog enumerates with PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS
(its booklet UI uses its own dropdown, not PrintDlgW like Notepad).
WINSPOOL_EnumPrintersW stripped CONNECTIONS and, when it was the
only flag, returned TRUE with zero printers. Result: Notepad
(PRINTER_ENUM_LOCAL) listed CUPS printers while Affinity showed
"No printers installed" on the same prefix.

Wine has no separate connection concept: every CUPS destination is
exposed as a local printer. Map CONNECTIONS to LOCAL instead of
returning empty. CONN|LOCAL behaviour is unchanged, and Wine's own
check_printer_setup fallback (LOCAL then CONNECTIONS) becomes
meaningful.

Reproduced with a virtual queue
(lpadmin -p AffinityTest -E -m raw -v socket://127.0.0.1:9100):
LOCAL L1 -> 1 printer, CONN-only L1 -> 0 printers before fix.

--- a/dlls/winspool.drv/info.c	2026-10-01 00:00:00.000000000 -0300
+++ b/dlls/winspool.drv/info.c	2026-10-08 00:00:00.000000000 -0300
@@ -4040,13 +4040,11 @@ static BOOL WINSPOOL_EnumPrintersW(DWORD
 	return TRUE;
 
     if (dwType & PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS) {
-        TRACE("ignoring PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS\n");
-        dwType &= ~PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS; /* we don't handle that */
-        if (!dwType) {
-            FIXME("We don't handle PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS\n");
-            return TRUE;
-        }
-
+        TRACE("mapping PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS to local CUPS printers\n");
+        dwType &= ~PRINTER_ENUM_CONNECTIONS;
+        /* Wine exposes every CUPS destination as local; there is no
+           separate connection namespace, so answer with local printers. */
+        dwType |= PRINTER_ENUM_LOCAL;
     }
 
     if (!((dwType & PRINTER_ENUM_LOCAL) || (dwType & PRINTER_ENUM_NAME))) {
